WEBVTT

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:04.100
What if the world's busiest shipping
shortcuts suddenly disappeared?

00:00:04.290 --> 00:00:05.540
Meet the Strait of Malacca,

00:00:05.630 --> 00:00:09.440
located between the Malay Peninsula
and the Indonesian island of Sumatra.

00:00:09.690 --> 00:00:13.020
It connects the Indian Ocean with
the South China Sea and the Pacific.

00:00:13.290 --> 00:00:16.780
Millions of barrels of oil pass
through this narrow route every day.

00:00:16.910 --> 00:00:20.740
Ships travelling between the Middle
East and East Asia depend heavily on it.

00:00:20.740 --> 00:00:23.910
If it were blocked, ships would
need longer alternative routes,

00:00:23.960 --> 00:00:26.290
increasing travel time and shipping costs.

00:00:26.550 --> 00:00:29.260
And that could affect everything
from fuel to electronics.

00:00:29.580 --> 00:00:33.810
Tomorrow, let's travel 4,500
years into India's past.

